{
  "dom_id": "step-q315550",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=(4t-7){e}^{t},$ where $t>0$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x.$\n\n$t\\in (${{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}}$)$",
  "worked_solution": "If the particle moves in the direction of increasing $x,$ then its velocity is positive. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((4t-7){e}^{t}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{t}+(4t-7){e}^{t} \\\\  & =(4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x$, we solve $v(t)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & >0 \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t} & >0 \\\\ 4t-3 & >0 \\\\ t & >\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of increasing $x$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (\\frac{3}{4},\\infty ).\n$$",
